  "analysis": [
    {
      "label": "Context",
      "text": "The final was level at 1–1 after goals from Benzema and Mané. Zidane sent on Bale in place of Isco, and within a few minutes Real Madrid were back in front."
    },
    {
      "label": "Build-up",
      "text": "Madrid moved the ball patiently through midfield before finding Marcelo in space on the left. With Liverpool's defenders drawn towards the middle, Marcelo had time to pick out a cross into the box."
    },
    {
      "label": "The technique",
      "text": "The cross arrived slightly behind Bale, too awkward for a header or a normal volley. Bale leapt, turned away from goal and struck a left-footed overhead kick, keeping the ball down enough to hit the target."
    },
    {
      "label": "The finish",
      "text": "The shot flew into the top corner beyond Karius, who had no time to react from that range. Bale later added Madrid's third from long range as Madrid won 3–1."
    }
  ],
  "note": "Reconstructed from memory of the footage: Marcelo's cross from the left and Bale's overhead kick into the top corner past Karius are as they happened, but the passes before Marcelo, the Liverpool defenders' positions, which top corner, and kit trim and goalkeeper colours are approximate. Commentary is original, not the broadcast."
